  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe pattern of PR #2355 (Haas) goes into five more posts. The dwell is part of the cycle signature. A changed dwell writes G80 and a new cycle block with its own P. A hole with the same dwell keeps the modal short form (bare X Y).\n\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`, `assets/posts/mazak.cps`, `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: the signature of G82 and G89 includes the dwell in ms.\n- `assets/posts/grblhal.cps`, `assets/posts/tormach.cps`: the signature of G82, G86 and G89 includes the dwell in seconds. These two posts also write a G86 P, so G86 has the same defect.\n- All five posts: a back-bore with a dwell of 0 posts G85 (feed in, feed out), not G89 with no P. A drill with a dwell of 0 posts G81, as before. Thus a dwell of 0 writes no P word, and no old P stays active.\n\nThe PR #2351 G83 dwell refusal and the PR #2048 behaviour do not change.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Fanuc G82/G89 formats give P as the dwell; G85 has no P. No public source that we read confirms `P0` on Fanuc, Mazak or Doosan. Thus G85 is used for a zero-dwell back-bore. G85 is the same motion as G89 with no dwell.\n- LinuxCNC G-code reference: G82, G86 and G89 take P in seconds, G85 has no P. The LinuxCNC interpreter (`interp_cycles.cc`, `convert_cycle_xy`) keeps the last P (`cycle_p`) for a block without P in the same motion mode. It refuses a G82, G86 or G89 block without P after G80.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/2360-dwell-cycle-signature.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/post/tests/dwell_cycles_modal_p.rs` (5 tests, each over the five posts; the G86 test over grblHAL and Tormach):\n\n- `g82_rewrites_p_when_the_dwell_changes`\n- `g82_then_g89_each_hole_posts_its_own_p`\n- `dwell_to_zero_leaves_no_p_active`\n- `same_dwell_keeps_the_open_group` (guard: the short form stays)\n- `linuxcnc_family_g86_rewrites_p_when_the_dwell_changes`\n\nOn the post files of `origin/main`, 4 of the 5 tests fail. `same_dwell_keeps_the_open_group` passes on both, as it must.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`: 80 test binaries, 674 tests passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance`: 7 passed. No golden `.nc` changed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real Fanuc, Mazak, Doosan, grblHAL or PathPilot control ran the output.\n- The other `camcraft-app` post suites did not run. No golden changed.\n- A zero-dwell G86 on grblHAL and Tormach still posts with no P. The LinuxCNC interpreter refuses it after G80. That is filed as #2362 (`P3`) and is not in this PR.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc, Mazak, Doosan, grblHAL and Tormach posts write each hole's own dwell P on G82 and G89 (and G86 on grblHAL and Tormach); a back-bore with no dwell posts G85.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2360\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
